# Fonts are binary. Without this, git's autocrlf on Windows can rewrite bytes
# inside a .woff2 and the font fails to decode with no useful error — the page
# just silently falls back. Auto-detection already gets this right today; this
# makes it guaranteed rather than lucky.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# Notebooks and images likewise
*.ipynb -text
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.pt    binary
*.bin   binary
